{
  "company_name": "IronPulse Manufacturing",
  "industry": "Machinery",
  "use_case": "Industrial asset health monitoring and predictive maintenance",
  "space_title": "IronPulse Manufacturing - Asset Health Monitor 🔧",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Machinery\n\n**Use case:** Asset Health & Predictive Maintenance\n\nIronPulse Manufacturing — condition-monitoring analytics for 20 industrial assets (compressors, pumps, turbines, gearboxes, motors) across utilities, process, power gen, milling, and conveyor areas. Reliability Engineers and Plant Managers track vibration, bearing temperature, and computed health indices day-to-day; the VP of Operations and CFO use it to quantify avoided downtime, prediction ROI, and maintenance spend versus availability targets.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Health index (0–100) — composite condition score; <50 triggers planned intervention\n- Vibration velocity (mm/s) — ISO 10816 zones: Good <4.5, Alert 4.5–11.2, Danger ≥11.2\n- Remaining useful life (days) — predictive horizon to plan parts and labor\n- Asset availability (%) — world-class target ≥90%, leaders 95%+\n- Mean time between failures (MTBF) — heavy rotating equipment benchmark 4,000–8,000 hrs\n- Unplanned downtime hours — direct production-loss driver\n- Prediction catch rate — % of failures detected before breakdown (target ≥60%)\n- Maintenance cost ($) per asset — capex deferral and opex budget input\n\n**Data sources**\n- `condition_readings` — daily vibration, bearing/oil temperature, health index, RUL per asset\n- `failure_events` — recorded failures with mode, detection method, severity, downtime, repair cost\n- `asset_health_monthly` — monthly availability, maintenance cost, predicted-failure catches, downtime",
  "schema_basename": "mach_asset_health",
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "condition_readings",
      "description": "Condition monitoring readings from industrial assets including vibration, temperature, oil analysis, and computed health indices.",
